TASK 1: LINEAR SEARCH

Aim:
To search an element in an array using Linear Search.

Theory:
Linear Search is the simplest searching technique in which each element of the array is checked one by one until the desired element is found.

Result:
The given element was searched successfully using Linear Search.

--------------------------------------------------

TASK 2: BINARY SEARCH

Aim:
To search an element in a sorted array using Binary Search.

Theory:
Binary Search divides the array into two halves repeatedly until the required element is found. It works only on sorted arrays.

Result:
The element was searched successfully using Binary Search.

--------------------------------------------------

TASK 3: REVERSE ARRAY

Aim:
To reverse the elements of an array.

Theory:
Array elements can be displayed in reverse order by traversing the array from the last index to the first index.

Result:
The array elements were displayed in reverse order successfully.